      "pins": ["PR9.SDA", "PR9.SCL", "PR9.VCC", "H7.3", "H7.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0062", "NET0079", "+5V"],
      "observed": "In the WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES block the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR9) is connected through header H7 (PB_1.25mm) onto the main I2C bus: its SDA/SCL pins land on NET0062/NET0079 and its VCC on +5V. No HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor or trigger/echo GPIO nets appear anywhere in the schematic; the only 'Water Height Sensor' drawn is the LiDAR.",
      "expected": "Per the spec the LiDAR is documentation-only and must not be wired: 'all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design' (§4.3). The water-level sensor that is 'actually wired and actually used by firmware is an HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor read on two ESP32 GPIOs' (§4.4).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 ... all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design (§4.3)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the water-level sensing that is actually wired and actually used by firmware is an HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor read on two ESP32 GPIOs (§4.4)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1, WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES: PR9 LiDAR -> H7 -> NET0062 / NET0079 / +5V; no ultrasonic symbol present"}
      ],
      "impact": "Automatic top-off level measurement as the firmware expects (ultrasonic on two GPIOs) has no hardware on this board, so ATO water-level sensing would not function as intended; meanwhile an unmanaged LiDAR device is placed on the shared I2C bus.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component",
      "components": ["T2"],
      "pins": ["T2.1", "T2.2", "T2.3"],
      "nets": ["NET0083", "NET0013", "NET0008"],
      "observed": "The ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch is drawn as T2 = A03400A (SOT-23, 30 V N-MOSFET).",
      "expected": "The spec's component table assigns the ATO valve switch to an AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET): 'T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch'. A 30 V SOT-23 part on a 24 V inductive load has only marginal Vds headroom versus the intended higher-rated DFN device.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 1/3, ATO Valve: T2 A03400A driven via R15/NET0083 and level-shifter T8"}
      ],
      "impact": "If AON6407 was selected for its higher voltage/current rating, substituting a 30 V SOT-23 AO3400A reduces margin on the 24 V inductive valve load, risking avalanche/stress on flyback transients.",
      "confidence": 0.25
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power train, isolators (pH/EC isolated, RTD unisolated), three TMC2209 dosing drivers with 110 m sense and shared UART, float interlocks, TVS/fuse and buck/LDO values all match the spec. The main deviation is the water-level sensing: the schematic wires the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR9/H7) onto the I2C bus and omits the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor that the spec states is the actually-wired and firmware-used level sensor, which would break ATO level sensing; a secondary, lower-confidence concern is the ATO valve MOSFET being an A03400A instead of the specified AON6407."
}

